urname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Length of stay, jaundice, and hospital readmission</article-title><source>Pediatrics</source><year>1998</year><volume>101</volume><fpage>995</fpage><lpage>998</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9606225</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-tcrm-5-0247"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Volpe</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name></person-group><source>Neurology of the Newborn</source><publisher-loc>Philadelphia, PA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>WB Saunders</publisher-name><year>1995</year><fpage>490</fpage><lpage>514</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b10-tcrm-5-0247"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Newman</surname><given-names>TB</given-names></name><name><surname>Klebanoff</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Neonatal hyperbilirubinemia and long-term outcome: another look at the Collaborative Perinatal Project</article-title><source>Pediatrics</source><year>1993</year><volume>92</volume><fpage>651</fpage><lpage>657</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8414851</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-tcrm-5-0247"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maisels</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gifford</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Antle</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Normal serum bilirubin levels in the newborn and the effect of breast feeding</article-title><source>Pediatrics</source><year>1986</year><volume>78</volume><fpage>837</fpage><lpage>843</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3763296</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12-tcrm-5-0247"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname